-- title:
--   Finite time bound for the complete block-source catalog
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,c\in\mathbb N$, set $W=512hJ$, and assume $c\le W$. Let $C$ be the number of source occurrences, namely the local schedule length raised to the $J$th power. Let $G(h,J)$ be the defined per-occurrence factor for the retained-source program, and put
--   $$F(h,J)=G(h,J)+1120+300(J+1)(\lfloor\log_2(C+1)\rfloor+2),\qquad D(W,c)=\sum_{i=0}^{c}\binom Wi.$$
--   The catalog constructor's explicit time function satisfies
--   $$T_{\rm catalog}(h,J,c)\le(C+1)F(h,J)(D(W,c)+1).$$
--   The factor $G$ includes retained-row generation and its finite arithmetic costs; the added term covers construction of the occurrence-digit arrays.
--
--   This packages the complete catalog cost as an occurrence count times a downset-size allowance and a finite parameter factor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBlockSourceCatalogProgram.lean#L34-L58

